WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:29.060
A 67-year-old BC retiree's TFSA trounce the market by buying during panics. This is Modern Investing Techniques, episode 229. After the tape, a hybrid income sleeve for registered accounts, a simulated high dividend hold, then the reviews, two account tools, and a down-day buying rule. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor,

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:34.120
and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:39.820
Firm October inflation in the United States lifted equities even as it repriced a December hike,

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:47.740
a step firmer than the open fed path question we left yesterday. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,619,

00:00:47.740 --> 00:01:02.240
up 1.3%, the NASDAQ composite at 25,466, up 1.6%, and the TSX composite at 36,412, up 0.7%.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:09.440
That NASDAQ print sits 9.60% higher year to date, and 13.82% higher since the practice

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:16.620
portfolio opened on March 16th, 2026. Technology and energy led the TSX advance, while the

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.940
the Canadian dollar weakened to $0.70 US.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:26.800
An October US consumer price index or CPI rose 0.4% month over month, with core CPI

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:33.060
up 0.3%, a pairing that has markets paying for a December fed move of at least 25 basis

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:33.420
points.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:41.120
The December crude oil contract rose $0.49 to $86.53 a barrel, and the December gold

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:49.443
contract fell $29.70 to $4,000 in 50 cents an ounce. Guaranteed investment certificates

00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:55.203
or GICs paired with dividend growth holdings inside a tax-free savings account or TFSA

00:01:55.563 --> 00:02:01.003
build a tax-free income stream in Motley Fools working that balances a locked yield against

00:02:01.003 --> 00:02:08.823
inflation protection. The cumulative maximum TFSA room stands at $109,000 in 2026 for anyone

00:02:08.823 --> 00:02:14.983
who has contributed every year since 2009, and the work split parks $50,000 in a 5-year

00:02:14.983 --> 00:02:24.123
GIC at 4.2% for $2,100 of annual tax-free interest, then pairs it with $59,000 in a diversified

00:02:24.123 --> 00:02:31.303
dividend exchange traded fund, or ETF, yielding 3.3% for another $1,947.

00:02:32.193 --> 00:02:38.403
Add those two checks and you are looking at roughly $4,047 of annual tax-free cash, which

00:02:38.403 --> 00:02:42.323
is the whole point of running both sleeves inside the wrapper rather than an

00:02:42.323 --> 00:02:47.243
taxable account. Think of it as splitting a winter wood pile. One lock shed you

00:02:47.243 --> 00:02:52.323
cannot open for five years, which is the non-cashable GIC, and a wood lot that

00:02:52.323 --> 00:02:56.783
keeps growing new trees, which is the rising dividend stream. Implementation

00:02:56.783 --> 00:03:02.623
uses a self-directed TFSA at Questrade or WealthSimple, sets a 60-40 allocation

00:03:02.623 --> 00:03:07.503
target, turns on automatic distribution reinvestment, and reviews the mix once

00:03:07.503 --> 00:03:13.083
a quarter. Staggering GIC maturities across several years so a slice rolls every 12 months

00:03:13.423 --> 00:03:18.683
is how you keep from being stuck with one-stale rate. The mix has delivered steady real returns

00:03:18.683 --> 00:03:24.143
when inflation stayed below 3%, and it lags a pure equity book in a strong bull market,

00:03:24.583 --> 00:03:29.863
which is the trade-off you accept in writing. Rate reset risk is the ugly case. If yields

00:03:29.863 --> 00:03:35.563
fall hard and GIC renewals print below inflation, purchasing power erodes inside the registered

00:03:35.563 --> 00:03:40.403
to count even though the interest itself is untaxed, and the non-cashable term removes

00:03:40.403 --> 00:03:43.143
any chance to reallocate if something better appears.

00:03:43.943 --> 00:03:48.683
Dividend names let you sell the same day in an emergency, but they also take mark to market

00:03:48.683 --> 00:03:49.123
hits.

00:03:49.643 --> 00:03:55.983
Endbridge near $67 after a slide from 80, despite 31 consecutive years of dividend increases,

00:03:56.443 --> 00:04:01.063
is the reminder that even a veteran payer can test an income thesis with a sharp drawdown.

00:04:01.063 --> 00:04:08.561
XEI on the TSX is today's simulated weekly hold, a $1,000 paper position in the eye shares

00:04:08.561 --> 00:04:14.841
S&amp;P TSX composite high dividend index ETF, entered at the next session's open and scored

00:04:14.841 --> 00:04:17.301
against the NASDAQ over its own five sessions.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:23.121
It is the dividend growth sleeve of that GIC and dividend hybrid, one ticker instead of

00:04:23.121 --> 00:04:28.301
a basket of single stock picks, so the rules-based record can measure whether the income approach

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:30.781
adds anything over the matched NASDAQ window.

00:04:31.361 --> 00:04:36.061
The catalyst is a monthly distribution from financials, energy, and utilities holdings,

00:04:36.361 --> 00:04:41.041
with a management expense ratio, or MER, of 0.22%.

00:04:41.041 --> 00:04:43.801
Cheap enough that the yield is not being eaten by fees.

00:04:44.321 --> 00:04:49.221
The technical read is a trade near recent support after a broader pullback, and the volume

00:04:49.221 --> 00:04:51.041
filter is not confirming a rebound.

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:54.341
So we are not treating tape strength as a supporting factor.

00:04:54.341 --> 00:05:00.281
The stop sits 8% below entry and caps the loss at $80 on the $1000 position.

00:05:00.781 --> 00:05:05.621
The invalidation I am naming before any fill is a daily close under the 50 session moving

00:05:05.621 --> 00:05:09.621
average, which would kill the thesis even if the stop has not been tagged.

00:05:10.021 --> 00:05:15.921
The target is plus 2 to plus 4% over 5 sessions if yield support holds, and confidence is

00:05:15.921 --> 00:05:20.121
medium because yield and sector mix line up while volume confirmation is missing.

00:05:20.121 --> 00:05:25.081
The sector rotation confirmation rule from the last dividend hold is in force here.

00:05:25.561 --> 00:05:28.101
Energy led the TSX in the session just closed.

00:05:28.521 --> 00:05:32.941
A partial pass, while financials and utilities sit on the wrong side of a December hike

00:05:32.941 --> 00:05:36.381
reprise, so this stays medium and does not get an upgrade.

00:05:36.961 --> 00:05:41.761
This is a simulated trade for learning purposes, no real money, and the only thing to watch

00:05:41.761 --> 00:05:45.981
on the first session is whether that moving average in validation even comes into view.

00:05:45.981 --> 00:05:52.770
EFX on the TSX was the last weekly hold, a valuation entry on a Canadian energy services

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:57.550
name, simulated from Thursdays open through Wednesdays close across five sessions.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:08.390
We simulated buying at $28.25 and exiting at $28.80, a gain of 1.95% or $19.47 on the

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:09.470
$1,000 position.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:14.290
The NASDAQ over those same five sessions fell 0.36%.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:18.170
So, the matched window alpha was plus 2.31%.

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:22.690
Stated confidence was medium, the daily close below the 50 session moving average and

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:26.630
validation never came close, and the 8% stop was not reached.

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:31.970
Medium fit the mixed tape of dividend support against sector rotation pressure, which is why

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:33.570
the stop never had worked to do.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:38.570
Require sector rotation confirmation before entering any dividend name already showing

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:39.490
relative weakness.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:44.496
Wellth Simple's contribution room tracker, which the Globe and Mail has walked through,

00:06:45.136 --> 00:06:51.216
pulls Canada Revenue Agency, or CRA, data automatically, and shows remaining 2026 room

00:06:51.216 --> 00:06:57.736
plus projected 2027 room after each deposit. Canadian investors use that running total to plan

00:06:57.736 --> 00:07:03.676
a GIC or dividend buy without tripping over contribution penalties, and it updates in real time

00:07:03.676 --> 00:07:09.096
when January room lands and when withdrawals go out. So you are not waiting on a CRA notice

00:07:09.096 --> 00:07:15.116
that arrives months late. Access is free inside any wealth simple TFSA after a bank account

00:07:15.116 --> 00:07:19.896
is linked, and the concrete step for the hybrid is checking remaining room before you wire

00:07:19.896 --> 00:07:28.324
the $50,000 GIC slice. Questtrade's ETF screener in Motley Fools walkthrough filters TSX listed

00:07:28.324 --> 00:07:34.944
funds by distribution yield, MER, and sector waiting so a high dividend name such as XEI can be

00:07:34.944 --> 00:07:40.624
isolated in under two minutes. The screen updates daily, saves, and alerts on yield changes.

00:07:41.104 --> 00:07:46.244
You can sort monthly versus quarterly distributions and export the list into a watch list to check

00:07:46.244 --> 00:07:51.644
holdings overlap with names you already sit on in the TFSA. That filter is the two-minute

00:07:51.644 --> 00:07:56.164
job before funding the equity sleeve, and it is free for questrate account holders.

00:07:56.604 --> 00:08:02.766
I have no financial relationship with wealth-simple or questrate. Sam Altman told a closed-door

00:08:02.766 --> 00:08:08.226
Samsung meeting that only open AI and anthropic are driving meaningful growth, with supply

00:08:08.226 --> 00:08:13.246
shocks expected before longer-run demand rises, and he warned executives of turbulence

00:08:13.246 --> 00:08:16.906
while still projecting a later surge in usage once supply eases.

00:08:17.406 --> 00:08:22.326
That mix argues for diversified AI exposure rather than a concentrated chip bet in the

00:08:22.326 --> 00:08:22.846
near-term.

00:08:23.783 --> 00:08:29.963
Dan Ives puts Nvidia at $300 US dollars with Jensen in the chair and $225 US dollars

00:08:29.963 --> 00:08:36.063
without him, a $75 gap that is single executive risk written in a price target, and he still

00:08:36.063 --> 00:08:39.783
calls the company foundational to the AI buildout through the current pressure.

00:08:40.363 --> 00:08:43.863
Position size stays smaller until that leadership question is cleaner.

00:08:44.944 --> 00:08:50.464
TSX futures edged lower as rate-sensitive Canadian sectors absorb the tighter policy reprice,

00:08:50.844 --> 00:08:55.644
and the same tape has some talk of a possible 50 basis point front-loaded December move

00:08:55.644 --> 00:08:56.964
rather than a single step.

00:08:56.964 --> 00:09:02.784
Fixed income sleeves inside a TFSA are worth a look before the next bank of Canada decision.

00:09:03.579 --> 00:09:09.519
Under the rules-based record that restarted on August 18, 2026, fixed five session holds,

00:09:10.099 --> 00:09:15.679
next open entries, stop or horizon exits, and no discretionary exits, matched window

00:09:15.679 --> 00:09:20.599
alpha versus the NASDAQ average plus 0.12% across 50 trades.

00:09:20.979 --> 00:09:24.059
Twenty-six of those 50 beat the index over their own window.

00:09:24.059 --> 00:09:32.419
The total across all positions stands at minus $257.10, and a T statistic of plus 0.14 means

00:09:32.419 --> 00:09:34.499
this is not yet distinguishable from luck.

00:09:35.179 --> 00:09:41.419
The full history since March 2026 covers 101 trades with a 52% win rate, and cumulative

00:09:41.419 --> 00:09:44.559
profit and loss of plus $39.57.

00:09:45.159 --> 00:09:49.763
A listener can take the pick, the date, and the stop, and reproduce every number.

00:09:49.763 --> 00:09:54.443
The method is still learning from mixed dividend setups and that sector rotation filter.

00:09:54.843 --> 00:09:59.923
You hold a large cap Canadian name in your TFSA that just dropped 12% on an unexpected

00:09:59.923 --> 00:10:05.303
sector shock, which is the exact setup that retiree faced more than once, and the question

00:10:05.303 --> 00:10:07.203
is whether you add, sit, or cut.

00:10:07.603 --> 00:10:12.303
What would you do with a preset add already written down, versus waiting for a perfect bottom

00:10:12.303 --> 00:10:13.083
you will not get?

00:10:13.663 --> 00:10:17.043
Pause on that for a beat because the mechanism is not timing skill.

00:10:17.043 --> 00:10:22.263
Over the decade in the Globe and Mail profile, that account compounded ahead of its benchmark

00:10:22.263 --> 00:10:24.403
by enough to matter for retirement income.

00:10:24.863 --> 00:10:28.623
And the working step was adding only after prices had already fallen hard.

00:10:29.143 --> 00:10:30.103
Never chasing strength.

00:10:30.763 --> 00:10:35.803
The tax-free compounding is what turns a temporary dislocation into a permanent basis improvement.

00:10:36.283 --> 00:10:41.163
No capital gains tax on the recovery sale, so the full bounce stays in the account instead

00:10:41.163 --> 00:10:46.143
of losing 25% or more to tax on each cycle the way a taxable account would.

00:10:46.143 --> 00:10:51.143
The pro habit is to pre-define a fixed dollar amount, or a percentage of new contribution

00:10:51.143 --> 00:10:57.403
room, and deploy it only on days the TSX is down at least 1.5%, which takes the mood

00:10:57.403 --> 00:10:58.083
out of the click.

00:10:58.623 --> 00:11:01.503
The misconception is that panic buying needs a perfect low.

00:11:02.063 --> 00:11:06.543
The actual edge is showing up whenever broad fear prints, and a measure of luck in the

00:11:06.543 --> 00:11:08.903
specific name still sat inside that result.

00:11:09.423 --> 00:11:14.903
Keep a watch list of large caps you already hold in the TFSA, set calendar alerts for quarterly

00:11:14.903 --> 00:11:19.563
room additions, and let those alerts coincide with tape weakness rather than with a hot

00:11:19.563 --> 00:11:19.943
open.

00:11:20.849 --> 00:11:26.809
Open your TFSA list, flag any name down more than 10% from average cost, write the date

00:11:26.809 --> 00:11:32.789
at first cross that line, and decide whether the next 1.5% TSX down day is when that fixed

00:11:32.789 --> 00:11:34.189
dollar amount goes to work.

00:11:34.669 --> 00:11:40.069
Before we wrap, the simulated XEI hold is set to enter at the next session's open, and

00:11:40.069 --> 00:11:44.069
I will be watching whether that 50 session moving average even appears on day 1.

